  "term": "ataxic dysarthria",
  "definition": "Ataxic dysarthria is a speech disorder seen in some degenerative neurological and movement conditions, especially cerebellar ataxia. It reflects the underlying brain disease and can be distinguished from both normal speech and hypokinetic dysarthria.",
